Open the bucket's Management tab
S3 console mein leigostorage-prod bucket click karo. Top pe tabs dikhenge — Objects, Properties, Permissions, Metrics, Management. 'Management' tab pe click karo.
2
Create a Lifecycle rule
Management tab mein 'Lifecycle rules' section dikhega. 'Create lifecycle rule' button pe click karo.
3
Name the rule and set scope
Rule name do — jaise 'intelligent-tiering-all-objects'. Scope mein 'Apply to all objects in the bucket' select karo. Confirmation checkbox tick karo jo aayega.
4
Select the rule action
'Lifecycle rule actions' mein scroll karo. 'Move objects between storage classes' checkbox tick karo.
5
Choose Intelligent-Tiering and set days
Storage class transition dropdown mein 'Intelligent-Tiering' select karo. 'Days after object creation' mein 0 daalo — matlab objects upload hote hi automatically tier hone lagenge. (0 allowed hai Intelligent-Tiering ke liye.)
6
Save the rule
Bottom mein 'Create rule' click karo. Rule active ho jaayega. Existing 5.2 TB data bhi is rule ke under aane lagega — AWS next lifecycle evaluation cycle mein apply karega (usually 24 hrs).
7
Enable optional archive tiers (recommended)
Better savings ke liye: bucket ke Properties tab mein jaao → 'Intelligent-Tiering Archive configurations' → 'Create configuration'. Archive Access tier ke liye 90 days set karo, Deep Archive Access ke liye 180 days. Yeh cold data ko aur neeche tier karega (~68% cheaper than Standard).
